advance sales means an enormous amount of early demand is being cleared off the books immediately. When theatres return to st..."}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 154], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 154, "author": member:pintofmild, "at": d"2019-05-01T18:51:00.000Z", "body": "Dead right kookaburra, no casual punter is braving a late finish mid-week now the superfans are done!", "quote": {"post": post:["endgame", 153], "text": "now that backlog is gone, no way busy families keep turning up late mid-week."}, "note": "I still reckon the mid-week drop will prove Avatar's record is completely safe from Endgame.", "state": {"position":"Monday's big take was just spillover from sold-out weekend screenings, and casual viewers won't turn up on late work nights, so Avatar's record is completely safe.","score":1,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"convinced by his explanation of weekend spillover demand"},{"member":"OffByOne","feeling":"agrees with his take on the four-hour cinema commitment on work nights"},{"member":"Punchcard","feeling":"values his steady common sense about waiting for settled figures"}],"commitments":["waiting for verified figures","meeting anyone around for a pint","keeping strictly quiet about plot spoilers"],"shift":"He is now firmly convinced by quasistatic that Monday's high gross was merely weekend spillover rather than genuine casual demand."}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "Avatar's box office status is safe from Avengers: Endgame box office record once initial queuing ends"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "Avatar's record is totally safe against Avengers: Endgame"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "Avengers: Endgame's opinion is physical duration remains the real operational ceiling for weekday admissions"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "PintOfMild's opinion is TheyKnow is still making mountains out of tiny till errors when the rollout is basically done"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "PintOfMild's attitude is waiting for actuator and resolver logs before the software changeover"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "PintOfMild: \"Spot on with that!\""}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-30T21:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 63]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-05T11:32:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 178]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T11:07:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 56]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T23:17:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 72]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-01T12:48:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 100]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-04T21:09:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 38]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-18T19:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 1]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-18T19:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 1]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T11:18:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 11]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T08:24:00.000Z", "text": "That said, the international returns of $169 million on day one simply reflect the same front-loading we saw in the domestic presales. Meeting unprecedented demand across Korea, Australia, and Chin..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T17:06:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 117]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T21:39:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 119]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T22:32:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 121]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-30T19:00:00.000Z", "text": "1. A portion of that Monday gross inevitably represents deferred spillover from patrons who found weekend sessions entirely sold out, rather than newly converted casual viewers. 2. The structural b..."}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 155], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 155, "author": member:kookaburra99, "at": d"2019-05-02T09:04:00.000Z", "body": "Tuesday stayed up at 33 million though, which is massive, but it's still mostly the dedicated crowd burning through it before anyone spoils the ending for them. Casual folks aren't booking four-hour cinema outings right before work the next arvo.", "quote": NONE, "note": "I still reckon the late week numbers will drop off a cliff once the diehards finish seeing it.", "state": {"position":"Avatar's record is completely safe because Monday's numbers were just deferred weekend spillover, and ordinary families won't turn up for a four-hour cinema trip on mid-week nights.","score":0,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"OffByOne","feeling":"deeply persuaded by his clear analysis of the audience backlog"},{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"admires his clear explanation of weekend spillover versus casual demand"},{"member":"PintOfMild","feeling":"pleased he agrees with her view on ordinary families"}],"commitments":[],"shift":"Her belief that Avatar's record is safe remains firm, reinforced by agreement across the thread that Monday was merely deferred spillover."}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "Avengers: Endgame's opinion is physical duration remains the real operational ceiling for weekday admissions"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "Punchcard's opinion is healthy return, but represents deferred business from weekend sellouts rather than necessarily fresh footfall"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "kookaburra99's status is newbie"}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T08:07:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 19]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"1999-12-31T09:09:00.000Z", "text": "I have to head into the office later on for the dreaded evening shift, but I will definitely be popping back in here during my tea breaks to see how kookaburra99 and the Aussies are getting on. Kee..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T00:01:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 120]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T07:21:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 144]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T23:43:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 77]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-02T01:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 113]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-24T03:31:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 85]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-02T06:52:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 13]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-07T06:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 115]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T02:23:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 6]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-19T05:51:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 8]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-22T05:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 34]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-23T09:48:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 55]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-24T03:13:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 66]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-25T00:20:00.000Z", "text": "Seeing China post over a hundred million on a Wednesday just proves how fast they are chewing through the crowds. If people are already walking out of the cinema worn down and bleary-eyed like kook..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T04:57:00.000Z", "text": "Once people go back to their regular routines on Monday, nobody has four spare hours on a work night to go sit through a three-hour marathon. You simply cannot maintain that kind of traffic without..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T08:24:00.000Z", "text": "That said, the international returns of $169 million on day one simply reflect the same front-loading we saw in the domestic presales. Meeting unprecedented demand across Korea, Australia, and Chin..."}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 156], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 156, "author": member:quasistatic, "at": d"2019-05-02T11:05:00.000Z", "body": "The reported $33.4 million for Tuesday is undeniably resilient, bringing the domestic running total to roughly $427 million. However, one should be cautious about declaring the enthusiast wave spent quite so abruptly.\n\nWhen standard seating fills to capacity over a weekend, that deferred pressure does not simply vanish within twenty-four hours. It ripples across several evenings as patrons finally secure desirable seats, particularly those anxious to avoid plot disclosures before the week ends. China reaching over 3 billion yuan on Wednesday demonstrates that same global momentum.\n\nUntil we observe how receipts behave once the film enters its second full weekend without the cushion of artificial hype, Avatar's long-term endurance remains a distant standard.", "quote": {"post": post:["endgame", 155], "text": "Tuesday stayed up at 33 million though, which is massive, but it's still mostly the dedicated crowd burning through it before anyone spoils the ending for them."}, "note": "kookaburra99 is too quick to declare the superfan backlog fully cleared after just one or two days.", "state": {"position":"Endgame remains unlikely to beat Avatar because weekday grosses primarily reflect deferred weekend backlog and front-loaded superfan demand rather than genuine casual walk-ins enduring a four-hour commitment.","score":1,"certainty":"medium","towards":[{"member":"Punchcard","feeling":"appreciates his level-headed distinction between deferred business and fresh casual footfall"},{"member":"OffByOne","feeling":"pleased with his sound grasp of operational capacity and deferred demand"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"surprised to see him agree sensibly for once on deferred spillover"}],"commitments":["seeing the film in Edinburgh with her nephew next week","waiting for settled weekday receipts across the rest of the week"]}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "kookaburra99's expectation is burning through pre-sales quickly guarantees a massive drop next week once ANZAC crowds clear out and casual moviegoers stay home"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "Avengers: Endgame's opinion is physical duration remains the real operational ceiling for weekday admissions"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "quasistatic: \"We should inspect the actual wording of the redraft before making dramatic claims.\""}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T15:33:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 24]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-30T09:43:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 50]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T18:14:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 151]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-30T09:54:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 40]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-06T05:54:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 82]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-06T15:28:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 107]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T06:03:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 9]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-22T06:20:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 36]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-22T17:29:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 39]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-24T11:15:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 71]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-25T07:51:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 84]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T04:57:00.000Z", "text": "Once people go back to their regular routines on Monday, nobody has four spare hours on a work night to go sit through a three-hour marathon. You simply cannot maintain that kind of traffic without..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T08:24:00.000Z", "text": "That said, the international returns of $169 million on day one simply reflect the same front-loading we saw in the domestic presales. Meeting unprecedented demand across Korea, Australia, and Chin..."}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-26T17:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 103]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T22:57:00.000Z", "text": "The true test begins once the regular punters have to decide if they fancy sitting in a dark room for over three hours on a Tuesday night after work. I loved it to bits, but asking folk to surrende..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-27T06:47:00.000Z", "text": "When those artificial time-slots disappear and the pre-booked enthusiasts return home, daily capacity will decline sharply. A film requires broad, sustained general interest across months to approa..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-30T19:00:00.000Z", "text": "1. A portion of that Monday gross inevitably represents deferred spillover from patrons who found weekend sessions entirely sold out, rather than newly converted casual viewers. 2. The structural b..."}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 157], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 157, "author": member:punchcard, "at": d"2019-05-02T12:26:00.000Z", "body": "A queue that large takes several evenings to work through, so let us see how the second weekend opens.", "quote": NONE, "note": "quasistatic is right to caution the younger members about declaring the enthusiast crowd finished too quickly.", "state": {"position":"Midweek returns remain strong as deferred weekend demand and spoiler-averse fans continue to clear through, so we must wait to see how the numbers hold up once the initial rush truly settles.","score":2,"certainty":"medium","towards":[{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"values his level-headed breakdown of how initial demand and backlog ripple across multiple weekdays"},{"member":"Sysop_Kev","feeling":"appreciates his steady focus on cleared receipts rather than napkin math"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"weary of his habit of borrowing trouble and jumping to quick conclusions"}],"commitments":[],"shift":"He notes the robust Tuesday returns but shares the view that clearing the backlog of committed fans ripples across several days before genuine casual demand can be judged."}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "Avengers: Endgame's opinion is physical duration remains the real operational ceiling for weekday admissions"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "kookaburra99's expectation is burning through pre-sales quickly guarantees a massive drop next week once ANZAC crowds clear out and casual moviegoers stay home"}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-26T15:23:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 7]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T02:11:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 130]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2000-01-01T05:45:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 139]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T07:29:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 145]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2000-01-03T18:30:00.000Z", "text": "[quoting: \"Even when an odd glitch turns up - like those police breath-test units in Hong Kong this morning - the officers simply write the birth dates down in a notebook while the readings carry o..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-29T18:20:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 32]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T23:50:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 79]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-24T21:18:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 123]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-05T14:39:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 48]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-18T23:29:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 2]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-18T23:29:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 2]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-21T16:33:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 29]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-23T23:26:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 64]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-24T02:09:00.000Z", "text": "Those first reviews hitting ninety-eight percent today might help grease the wheels for this weekend, sure, but glowing press never paid for a seat on week three. Out in the real world, folks have ..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-24T23:29:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 77]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-27T06:47:00.000Z", "text": "When those artificial time-slots disappear and the pre-booked enthusiasts return home, daily capacity will decline sharply. A film requires broad, sustained general interest across months to approa..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-27T23:41:00.000Z", "text": "As quasistatic noted, satisfying sixty percent of your audience through advance sales means an enormous amount of early demand is being cleared off the books immediately. When theatres return to st..."}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 158], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 158, "author": member:pintofmild, "at": d"2019-05-02T15:45:00.000Z", "body": "Aye, once this second weekend lands we will see if anybody outside the die-hards is genuinely turning up.", "quote": NONE, "note": "I still think casual moviegoers will stay away once the die-hard fan rush cools off this weekend.", "state": {"position":"The massive early weekdays are just the huge initial backlog taking several evenings to work through, so casual crowds still won't turn up and Avatar's record won't be caught.","score":1,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"convinced by his breakdown of deferred weekday pressure"},{"member":"kookaburra99","feeling":"chummy agreement on casual punters avoiding mid-week late finishes"},{"member":"Punchcard","feeling":"appreciates his patient perspective on working through the queue"}],"commitments":["waiting for verified figures","meeting anyone around for a pint","keeping strictly quiet about plot spoilers"],"shift":"He feels further validated by the board that even strong Tuesday figures are just the remaining fan queue taking a few nights to clear."}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "Sysop_Kev: \"Sure look, we will see what the actual figures look like next week once the rush clears out.\""}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "Punchcard's opinion is healthy return, but represents deferred business from weekend sellouts rather than necessarily fresh footfall"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "PintOfMild: \"Spot on with that!\""}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-03T00:36:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 171]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2000-01-03T09:20:00.000Z", "text": "We have already seen examples over the weekend, such as the temporary glitch with Amtrak's tracking software, where automated fallbacks and manual procedures ensured normal operations continued wit..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2000-01-03T18:30:00.000Z", "text": "[quoting: \"Even when an odd glitch turns up - like those police breath-test units in Hong Kong this morning - the officers simply write the birth dates down in a notebook while the readings carry o..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-05T11:32:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 178]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T11:07:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 56]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T23:17:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 72]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-01T12:48:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 100]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-04T21:09:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 38]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-18T19:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 1]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-18T19:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 1]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T11:18:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 11]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-24T23:29:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 77]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T17:06:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 117]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T21:39:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 119]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-27T23:41:00.000Z", "text": "As quasistatic noted, satisfying sixty percent of your audience through advance sales means an enormous amount of early demand is being cleared off the books immediately. When theatres return to st..."}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-28T14:26:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 128]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T10:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 145]}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 159], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 159, "author": member:theyknow, "at": d"2019-05-02T17:48:00.000Z", "body": "Punchcard and quasistatic have the long view on this... That thirty-three million on Tuesday is just that same dam breaking a little slower than expected, folks. When you whip millions of fans into a frenzy over leaks, people scramble for whatever seat is left on Tuesday or Wednesday just to dodge the chatter online! That is pure FEAR driving ticket sales, not ordinary families deciding they suddenly fancy a four-hour evening haul on a work night. Once this opening wave finishes burning through the pipeline, the second weekend will give us the real unvarnished picture. Avatar has nothing to fret about yet. :)", "quote": NONE, "note": "The massive weekday figures are just spoiler panic dragging out the initial backlog, and casual crowds will still desert it once the rush clears.", "state": {"position":"The massive weekday figures are merely the initial weekend backlog rippling through several nights to avoid spoilers, and regular audiences will still abandon it once the hype clears.","score":1,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"admires his sharp eye for how weekend backlog ripples across several evenings"},{"member":"Punchcard","feeling":"respects his steady patience in waiting for the second weekend"},{"member":"kookaburra99","feeling":"pleased he recognises that casual families will not turn up on work nights"}],"commitments":["taking nephew to see Endgame in Edinburgh next week","wait until auditoriums return to sensible capacity in Rotterdam before going"],"shift":"Rationalises strong Tuesday returns as deferred enthusiast backlog and spoiler fear rippling across several nights rather than genuine casual demand."}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "TheyKnow's opinion is believes Monday business is deferred spillover clearing the weekend backlog rather than new walk-ups, and late weeknight cinema visits will drop off due to the three-hour runn..."}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "PintOfMild's opinion is front-loaded pre-sales will dry up once regular work resumes on Monday"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "TheyKnow's attitude is holding breath until motor logs are verified"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "TheyKnow's attitude is quite content to sit back, let telemetry trickle in, and wait for raw current draws rather than getting ahead of data"}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-26T12:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 2]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T01:08:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 16]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-30T21:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 63]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T04:18:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 133]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-27T19:47:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 7]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-21T22:01:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 67]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-07T11:36:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 119]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T01:32:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 5]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-22T03:26:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 33]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-24T11:15:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 71]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-25T18:00:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 90]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T00:06:00.000Z", "text": "OffByOne sees it clearly... once you exhaust that built-in capacity by Sunday, the drop is going to hit like a brick wall. When an experience leaves paying customers feeling like they need physical..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T04:57:00.000Z", "text": "Once people go back to their regular routines on Monday, nobody has four spare hours on a work night to go sit through a three-hour marathon. You simply cannot maintain that kind of traffic without..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T08:24:00.000Z", "text": "That said, the international returns of $169 million on day one simply reflect the same front-loading we saw in the domestic presales. Meeting unprecedented demand across Korea, Australia, and Chin..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T22:57:00.000Z", "text": "The true test begins once the regular punters have to decide if they fancy sitting in a dark room for over three hours on a Tuesday night after work. I loved it to bits, but asking folk to surrende..."}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T03:41:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 141]}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 160], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 160, "author": member:pintofmild, "at": d"2019-05-02T20:21:00.000Z", "body": "Too true mate, everyone is terrified of having the ending ruined before Friday! You get desperate and grab a random Wednesday seat just to dodge social media. But once that panic settles down, Avatar is still a mountain to climb.", "quote": NONE, "note": "TheyKnow and I are definitely on the same page about spoiler panic padding out the weekday numbers.", "state": {"position":"The strong early weekday numbers are still just the massive fan backlog taking several days to clear out, meaning Avatar's record remains out of reach once normal audiences stay home.","score":1,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"in rare agreement about fan frenzy driving the weekday numbers"},{"member":"Punchcard","feeling":"trusts his steady perspective on waiting for the second weekend"},{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"appreciates his breakdown of how deferred pressure ripples across the week"}],"commitments":["waiting for verified figures","meeting anyone around for a pint","keeping strictly quiet about plot spoilers"],"shift":"He feels further confirmed in his scepticism now that the board agrees the high Tuesday returns are driven by spoiler panic rather than genuine casual interest."}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "PintOfMild: \"Spot on with that!\""}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "PintOfMild: \"replying to quasistatic (post #103)\""}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-31T09:09:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 79]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-31T22:58:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 117]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-03T00:36:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 171]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-05T11:32:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 178]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T11:07:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 56]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T23:17:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 72]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-01T12:48:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 100]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-04T21:09:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 38]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", "text": "United States's box office growth is 17% behind last year"}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-18T19:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 1]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-18T19:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 1]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T11:18:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 11]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-23T12:19:00.000Z", "text": "Running theatres at 4 a.m. isn't business as usual, it is an outright admission that they know their window is razor-thin. Like OffByOne said, once you burn up all those diehards in seventy-two hou..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T08:24:00.000Z", "text": "That said, the international returns of $169 million on day one simply reflect the same front-loading we saw in the domestic presales. Meeting unprecedented demand across Korea, Australia, and Chin..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-27T06:47:00.000Z", "text": "When those artificial time-slots disappear and the pre-booked enthusiasts return home, daily capacity will decline sharply. A film requires broad, sustained general interest across months to approa..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T17:06:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 117]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T21:39:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 119]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T10:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 145]}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 161], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 161, "author": member:quasistatic, "at": d"2019-05-02T22:33:00.000Z", "body": "The social media metrics reported today certainly illustrate that climate. Twitter noted over fifty million tweets regarding the film since January, with almost half generated during this past week alone. That level of intense online noise creates an obvious urgency among regular viewers to protect themselves from plot revelations before the working week concludes.\n\nHowever, urgency should not be mistaken for broader demographic expansion. What we are witnessing is simply a very wide, very anxious core audience distributing itself across five or six days rather than three. That process naturally props up mid-week box office tallies, but it remains finite by its very nature. Once that protective barrier of early viewings is established, the film must rely on ordinary word of mouth and repeat attendances from people who do not mind giving up an entire afternoon or evening.\n\nSurpassing a worldwide total of over two and a half billion dollars requires casual cinemagoers to turn out steadily well into June and July. We should have the first reliable sense of whether that footfall actually exists when the second weekend returns are tallied.", "quote": NONE, "note": "I remain convinced that the inflated weekday returns reflect spoiler anxiety rather than genuine casual interest.", "state": {"position":"Endgame remains unlikely to beat Avatar, as strong weekday receipts still reflect the multi-day clearance of pent-up demand and spoiler avoidance rather than genuine long-term casual footfall.","score":1,"certainty":"medium","towards":[{"member":"Punchcard","feeling":"respects his steady patience in waiting for the second weekend data"},{"member":"kookaburra99","feeling":"thinks they were too quick to declare the initial enthusiast rush exhausted after Monday"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"notes his melodramatic phrasing but agrees on the underlying dynamic of front-loaded panic"}],"commitments":["seeing the film in Edinburgh with her nephew next week","waiting for receipts from the second full weekend"],"shift":"She has clarified that the opening backlog takes several evenings to disperse rather than ending immediately after Monday."}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "Avatar's box office status is safe from Avengers: Endgame box office record once initial queuing ends"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "Avatar's record is totally safe against Avengers: Endgame"}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T15:33:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 24]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-30T09:43:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 50]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-30T21:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 63]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T18:14:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 151]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T20:12:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 157]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-30T09:54:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 40]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-06T05:54:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 82]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-06T15:28:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 107]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T06:03:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 9]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-22T06:20:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 36]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-22T17:29:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 39]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-24T11:15:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 71]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-25T06:11:00.000Z", "text": "What we are seeing across the early markets is simply extreme compression. When a release schedules screenings across twenty-four hours to satisfy months of pre-orders, it rapidly depletes the fini..."}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-25T07:51:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 84]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-25T16:11:00.000Z", "text": "The trade reports this afternoon indicate BookMyShow has now shifted some two and a half million advance tickets in India, with operators there also resorting to round-the-clock screenings to manag..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T08:24:00.000Z", "text": "That said, the international returns of $169 million on day one simply reflect the same front-loading we saw in the domestic presales. Meeting unprecedented demand across Korea, Australia, and Chin..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T09:52:00.000Z", "text": "When a film relies almost entirely on advance bookings, exhibitors clear the vast majority of their customer base during the opening seventy-two hours. Once that committed audience has attended, th..."}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-26T17:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 103]}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 162], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 162, "author": member:kookaburra99, "at": d"2019-05-03T00:45:00.000Z", "body": "totally agree on that. people just rushed out this week because the spoiler panic online was insane! once that fear is gone, casual crowds aren't going to spend entire weekends sitting through a three-hour film over and over. avatar still has nothing to worry about.", "quote": NONE, "note": "quasistatic's point about spoiler panic stretching the core crowd across the week makes total sense.", "state": {"position":"Avatar's record remains safe because strong mid-week numbers are just anxious fans spreading out across several days to avoid spoilers rather than true casual demand.","score":0,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"deeply convinced by his clear explanation of spoiler anxiety spreading demand"},{"member":"PintOfMild","feeling":"enjoys his down-to-earth agreement"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"surprised to find herself agreeing with his take on fan panic"}],"commitments":[],"shift":"Her confidence that Avatar's record is safe grew even stronger after seeing how spoiler avoidance explains the persistent mid-week ticket sales."}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "kookaburra99's status is newbie"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "quasistatic: \"We should inspect the actual wording of the redraft before making dramatic claims.\""}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T08:07:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 19]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-30T21:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 63]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T00:01:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 120]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T23:43:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 77]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-02T01:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 113]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-24T03:31:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 85]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-02T06:52:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 13]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-07T06:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 115]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", "text": "United States's box office growth is 17% behind last year"}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T02:23:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 6]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-19T05:51:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 8]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-19T06:03:00.000Z", "text": "My nephew has booked tickets for us in Edinburgh for the following week, so I shall be doing my best to avoid the leaks in the meantime. I am curious to see the actual Comscore returns once the wee..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-22T05:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 34]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-24T03:13:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 66]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-24T11:15:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 71]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T08:24:00.000Z", "text": "That said, the international returns of $169 million on day one simply reflect the same front-loading we saw in the domestic presales. Meeting unprecedented demand across Korea, Australia, and Chin..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-27T06:47:00.000Z", "text": "When those artificial time-slots disappear and the pre-booked enthusiasts return home, daily capacity will decline sharply. A film requires broad, sustained general interest across months to approa..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-05-02T22:33:00.000Z", "text": "However, urgency should not be mistaken for broader demographic expansion. What we are witnessing is simply a very wide, very anxious core audience distributing itself across five or six days rathe..."}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 163], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 163, "author": member:offbyone, "at": d"2019-05-03T05:33:00.000Z", "body": "The five-day dispersion pattern is precisely what one would anticipate under these conditions. The anxiety over plot disclosures merely flattened the initial attendance peak across Wednesday and Thursday instead of confining it to Sunday evening. That is simply the mechanical distribution of existing demand rather than new audience acquisition. \n\nA genuine challenge to historical records requires substantial uncommitted footfall across subsequent months, not merely an accelerated processing of the established base. As Punchcard observed, the second-weekend clearing data will provide the first uncorrupted baseline. Until those figures arrive, projecting lifetime parity with Avatar remains entirely premature. I still intend to wait until the local auditoriums here quiet down before attending.", "quote": NONE, "note": "I remain confident that once the spoiler-conscious crowd finishes clearing out, second-weekend returns will demonstrate Avatar's total is out of reach.", "state": {"position":"Endgame will not overtake Avatar because weekday returns merely reflect the multi-day dispersion of opening-weekend backlog and spoiler-avoidance rather than genuine demographic expansion.","score":1,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"respects his precise analytical distinction between urgent core audience dispersion and genuine market expansion"},{"member":"Punchcard","feeling":"appreciates his patient, disciplined focus on second-weekend clearinghouse metrics"},{"member":"kookaburra99","feeling":"pleased he grasps the mechanical reality of deferred demand and spillover"}],"commitments":["see the film in Rotterdam once the auditoriums empty out"]}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "OffByOne's opinion is the analysis regarding deferred spillover is entirely sound"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "Resolution 6B's opinion is merely an administrative delay according to OffByOne"}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T06:50:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 18]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T13:43:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 22]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-02T10:11:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 166]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T22:22:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 67]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-03T20:11:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 141]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-04T09:09:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 150]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-19T08:52:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 55]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-07T14:14:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 121]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", "text": "United States's box office growth is 17% behind last year"}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-25T06:11:00.000Z", "text": "What we are seeing across the early markets is simply extreme compression. When a release schedules screenings across twenty-four hours to satisfy months of pre-orders, it rapidly depletes the fini..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-25T06:11:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 83]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-25T20:50:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 91]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T04:57:00.000Z", "text": "Once people go back to their regular routines on Monday, nobody has four spare hours on a work night to go sit through a three-hour marathon. You simply cannot maintain that kind of traffic without..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T08:24:00.000Z", "text": "That said, the international returns of $169 million on day one simply reflect the same front-loading we saw in the domestic presales. Meeting unprecedented demand across Korea, Australia, and Chin..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T09:52:00.000Z", "text": "When a film relies almost entirely on advance bookings, exhibitors clear the vast majority of their customer base during the opening seventy-two hours. Once that committed audience has attended, th..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T05:30:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 112]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-27T06:47:00.000Z", "text": "When those artificial time-slots disappear and the pre-booked enthusiasts return home, daily capacity will decline sharply. A film requires broad, sustained general interest across months to approa..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-29T12:04:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 135]}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 164], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 164, "author": member:theyknow, "at": d"2019-05-04T01:49:00.000Z", "body": "OffByOne lays out the cold mechanics right there, folks... Look at the headlines shouting about 1.78 billion worldwide today and promising two billion by tomorrow night. Ask yourself why they are rushing to crown it before Saturday's receipts even hit the ledger! That is pure corporate public relations trying to build an aura of inevitability. All that has happened this week is fifty million panicked tweets pushing the existing herd through the turnstiles a day or two earlier... Once that artificial urgency evaporates, the studio has to face the music with regular folks who are not glued to their screens. When you factor in a three-hour run time in the middle of spring chores, casual families are simply going to stay home and wait for the disc. This second weekend will show the true DEPTH of that well, and I suspect it runs far shallower than the trades want you to believe. Avatar still holds the high ground, my friends. :)", "quote": {"post": post:["endgame", 163], "text": "The anxiety over plot disclosures merely flattened the initial attendance peak across Wednesday and Thursday instead of confining it to Sunday evening. That is simply the mechanical distribution of existing demand rather than new audience acquisition."}, "note": "They are shouting about two billion early just to cover for the steep drop coming this weekend once ordinary folks stay home.", "state": {"position":"The film's high weekday numbers are purely manufactured spoiler panic spreading the initial fan rush across the week, meaning the true drop-off will show in the second weekend.","score":1,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"pleased he clearly sees how online spoiler fear artificially inflates weekday totals"},{"member":"OffByOne","feeling":"approves of his rational focus on mechanical demand dispersion over actual growth"},{"member":"Punchcard","feeling":"values his patience for waiting on the second weekend baseline"}],"commitments":["taking nephew to see Endgame in Edinburgh next week","wait until auditoriums return to sensible capacity in Rotterdam before going"]}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "Avengers: Endgame's opinion is physical duration remains the real operational ceiling for weekday admissions"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "Avatar's box office status is safe from Avengers: Endgame box office record once initial queuing ends"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "TheyKnow's attitude is holding breath until motor logs are verified"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "TheyKnow's attitude is quite content to sit back, let telemetry trickle in, and wait for raw current draws rather than getting ahead of data"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "TheyKnow: \"That is why staying prepared at home is just practical wisdom, my friends.\""}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-26T12:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 2]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T01:08:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 16]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-30T21:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 63]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T04:18:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 133]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-27T19:47:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 7]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-21T22:01:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 67]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-07T11:36:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 119]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T01:32:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 5]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-25T06:11:00.000Z", "text": "What we are seeing across the early markets is simply extreme compression. When a release schedules screenings across twenty-four hours to satisfy months of pre-orders, it rapidly depletes the fini..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-25T16:11:00.000Z", "text": "The trade reports this afternoon indicate BookMyShow has now shifted some two and a half million advance tickets in India, with operators there also resorting to round-the-clock screenings to manag..."}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-25T18:00:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 90]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T08:24:00.000Z", "text": "That said, the international returns of $169 million on day one simply reflect the same front-loading we saw in the domestic presales. Meeting unprecedented demand across Korea, Australia, and Chin..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-27T06:47:00.000Z", "text": "When those artificial time-slots disappear and the pre-booked enthusiasts return home, daily capacity will decline sharply. A film requires broad, sustained general interest across months to approa..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-05-02T17:48:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 159]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-05-02T22:33:00.000Z", "text": "However, urgency should not be mistaken for broader demographic expansion. What we are witnessing is simply a very wide, very anxious core audience distributing itself across five or six days rathe..."}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 165], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 165, "author": member:kookaburra99, "at": d"2019-05-04T03:02:00.000Z", "body": "spot on really. hitting 1.78 billion already sounds crazy huge on paper, but it really is just every single marvel fan on earth cramming into the earliest session they could find. once this weekend sorts out who is actually left, avatar's run is going to look completely out of reach.", "quote": NONE, "note": "TheyKnow and OffByOne explained the front-loading so well that I am certain Avatar's total is safe.", "state": {"position":"Avatar's record is completely safe because the massive mid-week turnout was just existing fans rushing out early to avoid spoilers rather than genuine casual demand.","score":0,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"OffByOne","feeling":"appreciates how clearly he explained demand dispersion"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"finds herself agreeing with his points on corporate PR"},{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"deeply trusts his analysis of audience urgency"}],"commitments":[]}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "kookaburra99's status is newbie"}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T08:07:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 19]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-30T21:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 63]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"1999-12-31T15:56:00.000Z", "text": "The Boston hospital incident demonstrates precisely why audits are conducted; oversight worked as intended, and missing an administrative patch on a server is not an uncontrollable physical failure..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T00:01:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 120]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T07:21:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 144]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T23:43:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 77]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-02T01:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 113]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-24T03:31:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 85]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-02T06:52:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 13]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-07T06:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 115]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", "text": "United States's box office growth is 17% behind last year"}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T02:23:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 6]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-19T05:51:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 8]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-22T05:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 34]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-23T12:19:00.000Z", "text": "Running theatres at 4 a.m. isn't business as usual, it is an outright admission that they know their window is razor-thin. Like OffByOne said, once you burn up all those diehards in seventy-two hou..."}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-23T12:34:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 57]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-24T03:13:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 66]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-05-02T22:33:00.000Z", "text": "However, urgency should not be mistaken for broader demographic expansion. What we are witnessing is simply a very wide, very anxious core audience distributing itself across five or six days rathe..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-05-04T01:49:00.000Z", "text": "OffByOne lays out the cold mechanics right there, folks... Look at the headlines shouting about 1.78 billion worldwide today and promising two billion by tomorrow night. Ask yourself why they are r..."}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 166], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 166, "author": member:offbyone, "at": d"2019-05-04T06:01:00.000Z", "body": "Small correction: the running total reported yesterday was $1.786 billion, not 1.78. Omitting six million dollars is somewhat sloppy. Nevertheless, tracking estimates projecting two billion by tonight merely describe the mathematical ceiling of pre-booked sessions. The crucial metric remains the second-weekend percentage drop once Monday's actual ledger arrives.", "quote": NONE, "note": "TheyKnow continues to wrap straightforward capacity mathematics in needlessly melodramatic corporate conspiracy rhetoric.", "state": {"position":"Endgame will fall short of Avatar because its massive early numbers merely reflect extreme front-loading and backlog dispersion rather than long-term casual footfall.","score":1,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"Punchcard","feeling":"values his emphasis on waiting for objective second-weekend clearinghouse metrics"},{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"appreciates his rational distinction between demand compression and demographic expansion"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"wary of his hyperbolic conspiratorial rhetoric despite their shared conclusion"}],"commitments":["see the film in Rotterdam once the auditoriums quiet down"]}, "recalled": [{"kind": "private", "text": "OffByOne: \"OffByOne's private note to self, Wed Dec 29, 1999 3:08 pm GMT: The card terminal glitch in Britain provides concrete proof that retail software errors do not cascade into industrial para..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T06:50:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 18]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-30T21:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 63]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"1999-12-31T15:56:00.000Z", "text": "The Boston hospital incident demonstrates precisely why audits are conducted; oversight worked as intended, and missing an administrative patch on a server is not an uncontrollable physical failure..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-02T10:11:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 166]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T22:22:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 67]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-03T20:11:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 141]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-04T09:09:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 150]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-19T08:52:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 55]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-07T14:14:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 121]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", "text": "United States's box office growth is 17% behind last year"}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-24T11:15:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 71]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-25T06:11:00.000Z", "text": "What we are seeing across the early markets is simply extreme compression. When a release schedules screenings across twenty-four hours to satisfy months of pre-orders, it rapidly depletes the fini..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-25T06:11:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 83]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-25T20:50:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 91]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T08:24:00.000Z", "text": "That said, the international returns of $169 million on day one simply reflect the same front-loading we saw in the domestic presales. Meeting unprecedented demand across Korea, Australia, and Chin..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T05:30:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 112]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-29T12:04:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 135]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-05-03T05:33:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 163]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-05-04T01:49:00.000Z", "text": "OffByOne lays out the cold mechanics right there, folks... Look at the headlines shouting about 1.78 billion worldwide today and promising two billion by tomorrow night. Ask yourself why they are r..."}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 167], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 167, "author": member:quasistatic, "at": d"2019-05-04T20:08:00.000Z", "body": "Reaching two billion dollars so early would be an extraordinary commercial feat, certainly, but OffByOne is right that it still tells us little about longevity. A steep drop this weekend will demonstrate whether the well has emptied, or if ordinary cinemagoers are actually stepping in.", "quote": NONE, "note": "I still expect the second-weekend drop to expose the lack of casual audience, leaving Avatar secure.", "state": {"position":"Endgame remains unlikely to beat Avatar, as the massive running totals merely reflect accelerated advance demand from existing fans driven by spoiler panic rather than new casual audiences.","score":1,"certainty":"medium","towards":[{"member":"OffByOne","feeling":"values his precise, logistical focus on attendance distribution and hard numbers"},{"member":"Punchcard","feeling":"appreciates his patient, sensible focus on awaiting the second weekend results"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"finds his spin sensationalized even if his point about artificial urgency is partly sound"}],"commitments":["seeing the film in Edinburgh with her nephew next week","waiting for receipts from the second full weekend"]}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "quasistatic: \"We should inspect the actual wording of the redraft before making dramatic claims.\""}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T15:33:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 24]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-30T09:43:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 50]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-30T21:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 63]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T18:14:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 151]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T20:12:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 157]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-30T09:54:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 40]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-06T05:54:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 82]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-06T15:28:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 107]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", "text": "United States's box office growth is 17% behind last year"}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T06:03:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 9]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-22T06:20:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 36]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-22T17:29:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 39]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-26T17:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 103]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-29T20:58:00.000Z", "text": "The actual figures released earlier this evening confirmed a worldwide total of 1.222 billion dollars, which is certainly an immense volume of capital, but it does not alter the underlying mechanic..."}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T05:04:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 142]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T06:05:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 144]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-05-02T22:33:00.000Z", "text": "However, urgency should not be mistaken for broader demographic expansion. What we are witnessing is simply a very wide, very anxious core audience distributing itself across five or six days rathe..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-05-02T22:33:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 161]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-05-04T01:49:00.000Z", "text": "OffByOne lays out the cold mechanics right there, folks... Look at the headlines shouting about 1.78 billion worldwide today and promising two billion by tomorrow night. Ask yourself why they are r..."}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 168], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 168, "author": member:kookaburra99, "at": d"2019-05-05T04:05:00.000Z", "body": "sorry if this is a dumb question, but when do the proper monday figures usually drop for the weekend percentage? lol. dying to see if the drop is as massive as everyone reckons once the hype settles down!!", "quote": NONE, "note": "OffByOne is always so sharp with the exact figures.", "state": {"position":"Avatar's record is completely safe because the massive numbers so far just represent existing fans rushing to early screenings rather than genuine long-term interest from casual moviegoers.","score":0,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"OffByOne","feeling":"admires his precise breakdown of demand distribution"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"strongly agrees with his points on PR hype and spoiler panic"},{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"respects his clear assessment of casual audience stamina"}],"commitments":[],"shift":"She has become even more firmly convinced that the record is safe after seeing the others explain that the massive early numbers are just front-loaded fan frenzy."}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "kookaburra99's status is newbie"}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T08:07:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 19]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-31T03:16:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 73]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T00:01:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 120]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T05:22:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 136]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T07:21:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 144]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T23:43:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 77]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-02T01:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 113]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-24T03:31:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 85]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-02T06:52:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 13]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-07T06:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 115]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", "text": "United States's box office growth is 17% behind last year"}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T02:23:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 6]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-19T05:51:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 8]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-22T05:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 34]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-24T03:13:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 66]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-24T11:15:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 71]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T08:24:00.000Z", "text": "That said, the international returns of $169 million on day one simply reflect the same front-loading we saw in the domestic presales. Meeting unprecedented demand across Korea, Australia, and Chin..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-05-02T22:33:00.000Z", "text": "However, urgency should not be mistaken for broader demographic expansion. What we are witnessing is simply a very wide, very anxious core audience distributing itself across five or six days rathe..."}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 169], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 169, "author": member:theyknow, "at": d"2019-05-05T04:26:00.000Z", "body": "Usually you will get the studio estimates hitting the morning news by midday on Sunday, my friend, and then the actual, verified figures come down the pipe by Monday afternoon or Tuesday morning... That is when the real accounting gets laid on the table. \n\nWhether those early forecasts manage to nudge it across the two billion mark on paper this weekend or not, that only tells you how hard the early crowd got squeezed through the doors. A massive opening push is one thing, but sustaining that kind of traffic once the core fans have seen it twice is entirely different. An ordinary working person with a yard to mow or errands to run just is not going to carve out four hours on a nice spring afternoon unless they are truly hooked, and that is where the drop-off will show its teeth. Avatar had legs that carried it through snowstorms and steady repeat crowds for months on end... We will have our first honest look at whether this thing has any staying power once those Monday returns check in. :)", "quote": NONE, "note": "I will wait for the audited Monday numbers to see if the drop knocks the wind out of their sails before I head over to the cinema with my nephew.", "state": {"position":"The massive numbers are merely the front-loaded core fanbase rushed through by manufactured spoiler panic, meaning Avatar's record will remain safe once casual crowds decline the three-hour haul.","score":1,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"OffByOne","feeling":"admires his analytical breakdown of demand mechanics despite his pedantic corrections"},{"member":"kookaburra99","feeling":"pleased to see him agreeing and seeing through the corporate hype"},{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"appreciates his rational focus on longevity over early inflated metrics"}],"commitments":["taking nephew to see Endgame in Edinburgh next week","wait until auditoriums return to sensible capacity in Rotterdam before going"]}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "TheyKnow's attitude is quite content to sit back, let telemetry trickle in, and wait for raw current draws rather than getting ahead of data"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "TheyKnow's attitude is holding breath until motor logs are verified"}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-26T12:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 2]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T01:08:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 16]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-30T21:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 63]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T04:18:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 133]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-27T19:47:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 7]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-21T22:01:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 67]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-07T11:36:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 119]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T01:32:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 5]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-19T06:03:00.000Z", "text": "My nephew has booked tickets for us in Edinburgh for the following week, so I shall be doing my best to avoid the leaks in the meantime. I am curious to see the actual Comscore returns once the wee..."}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-25T18:00:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 90]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T22:57:00.000Z", "text": "The true test begins once the regular punters have to decide if they fancy sitting in a dark room for over three hours on a Tuesday night after work. I loved it to bits, but asking folk to surrende..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-27T23:41:00.000Z", "text": "As quasistatic noted, satisfying sixty percent of your audience through advance sales means an enormous amount of early demand is being cleared off the books immediately. When theatres return to st..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-29T20:58:00.000Z", "text": "The actual figures released earlier this evening confirmed a worldwide total of 1.222 billion dollars, which is certainly an immense volume of capital, but it does not alter the underlying mechanic..."}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T03:41:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 141]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T05:04:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 142]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T06:05:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 144]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-05-01T01:49:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 150]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-05-02T17:48:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 159]}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 170], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 170, "author": member:kookaburra99, "at": d"2019-05-05T04:52:00.000Z", "body": "that timeline makes a lot of sense. especially with regular folks who only go to the movies a few times a year. they might tag along for something easy, but convincing them to sit through three hours when they have work or family stuff on is a whole different story. avatar was such a standalone visual spectacle that people could just wander in without needing homework, whereas this is basically a giant finale for dedicated fans. once the diehards are done rewatching it, that massive wall is going to show up pretty fast. eager to see those actual receipts come through tomorrow.", "quote": NONE, "note": "TheyKnow explained the weekend reporting schedule really clearly.", "state": {"position":"Avatar's record is completely safe because the massive early numbers simply reflect fans rushing to avoid spoilers rather than genuine long-term appeal for casual audiences.","score":0,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"OffByOne","feeling":"admires his sharp and precise command of figures"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"appreciates his helpfulness and agrees on the lack of casual staying power"},{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"respects his clear thoughts on the need for casual audience stamina"}],"commitments":[]}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "kookaburra99's status is newbie"}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T08:07:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 19]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-31T03:16:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 73]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T00:01:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 120]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T07:21:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 144]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T23:43:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 77]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-02T01:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 113]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-24T03:31:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 85]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-07T06:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 115]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", "text": "United States's box office growth is 17% behind last year"}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T02:23:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 6]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-19T05:51:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 8]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-19T06:03:00.000Z", "text": "My nephew has booked tickets for us in Edinburgh for the following week, so I shall be doing my best to avoid the leaks in the meantime. I am curious to see the actual Comscore returns once the wee..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-20T11:42:00.000Z", "text": "Audited receipts are the only honest measure we have, my friend... You can already see how the numbers get pumped up early on when you look at the news from overseas this morning. Over in China, pr..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-22T05:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 34]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-24T03:13:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 66]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T05:04:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 142]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-05-04T01:49:00.000Z", "text": "OffByOne lays out the cold mechanics right there, folks... Look at the headlines shouting about 1.78 billion worldwide today and promising two billion by tomorrow night. Ask yourself why they are r..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-05-05T04:05:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 168]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-05-05T04:26:00.000Z", "text": "Whether those early forecasts manage to nudge it across the two billion mark on paper this weekend or not, that only tells you how hard the early crowd got squeezed through the doors. A massive ope..."}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 171], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 171, "author": member:offbyone, "at": d"2019-05-05T05:19:00.000Z", "body": "Monday afternoon will yield the actual receipts, which will confirm whether the projected decline materialises as expected.", "quote": NONE, "note": "I will inspect the verified Monday receipts to confirm the steep decline.", "state": {"position":"Endgame will not beat Avatar because early grosses only measure front-loaded fan demand, and Monday's verified second-weekend figures will reveal the steep drop typical of runtime-constrained films.","score":1,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"respects his steady focus on measurable longevity versus early noise"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"disapproves of his imprecise rounding despite agreeing on the drop-off"},{"member":"kookaburra99","feeling":"views as an amateur needing basic guidance on reporting schedules"}],"commitments":["see the film in Rotterdam once the auditoriums quiet down"]}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "Avatar's box office status is safe from Avengers: Endgame box office record once initial queuing ends"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "kookaburra99's expectation is burning through pre-sales quickly guarantees a massive drop next week once ANZAC crowds clear out and casual moviegoers stay home"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "Avengers: Endgame's opinion is physical duration remains the real operational ceiling for weekday admissions"}, {"kind": "private", "text": "OffByOne: \"OffByOne's private note to self, Wed Dec 29, 1999 3:08 pm GMT: The card terminal glitch in Britain provides concrete proof that retail software errors do not cascade into industrial para..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T06:50:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 18]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-30T21:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 63]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-02T10:11:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 166]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T22:22:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 67]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-03T20:11:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 141]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-04T09:09:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 150]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-19T08:52:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 55]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-07T14:14:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 121]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-21T04:09:00.000Z", "text": "Chores, yard work, grocery runs, getting the kids to ball games... all that real life stuff adds up fast on a weekend, my friend. When a film demands over three hours of sitting still, not to menti..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-24T21:36:00.000Z", "text": "Avatar could sustain modest theatre occupancies over months because it slotted easily into standard evening slots and drew people who were completely unbothered by continuity. Endgame is consuming ..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-25T06:11:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 83]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-25T20:50:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 91]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T09:52:00.000Z", "text": "When a film relies almost entirely on advance bookings, exhibitors clear the vast majority of their customer base during the opening seventy-two hours. Once that committed audience has attended, th..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T05:30:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 112]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-29T12:04:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 135]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-05-03T05:33:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 163]}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 172], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 172, "author": member:pintofmild, "at": d"2019-05-05T08:07:00.000Z", "body": "Spot on about the homework aspect, mate! You can't just drag your auntie along to film number twenty-two when she hasn't seen the rest, especially for three hours. The diehards did their bit last week, so let us see what the actual cleared receipts say tomorrow afternoon.", "quote": {"post": post:["endgame", 170], "text": "avatar was such a standalone visual spectacle that people could just wander in without needing homework, whereas this is basically a giant finale for dedicated fans."}, "note": "I reckon the need to have seen twenty-one other films first will kill off any casual interest once tomorrow's numbers come in.", "state": {"position":"Endgame's huge numbers are just the fan rush being cleared out fast, and ordinary punters won't commit to a three-hour film once the hype dies down, keeping Avatar's record safe.","score":1,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"OffByOne","feeling":"respects his precise breakdown of front-loaded demand"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"agrees that casual crowds won't give up a spring afternoon"},{"member":"kookaburra99","feeling":"shares the friendly anticipation for the Monday figures"}],"commitments":["waiting for verified figures","meeting anyone around for a pint","keeping strictly quiet about plot spoilers"],"shift":"His view is unchanged as he happily goes along with the forum consensus that casual audiences will drop off sharply after this weekend."}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "John Koskinen: \"Even Koskinen himself said Monday is going to be the real test, my friend\""}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "PintOfMild's attitude is waiting for actuator and resolver logs before the software changeover"}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2000-01-03T09:20:00.000Z", "text": "We have already seen examples over the weekend, such as the temporary glitch with Amtrak's tracking software, where automated fallbacks and manual procedures ensured normal operations continued wit..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-05T11:32:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 178]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T11:07:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 56]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T23:17:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 72]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-01T12:48:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 100]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-04T21:09:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 38]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-18T19:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 1]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-18T19:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 1]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T11:18:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 11]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-23T23:26:00.000Z", "text": "We will only discover whether the title is genuinely in jeopardy once this first rush subsides and the actual audited receipts arrive across ordinary weeks of everyday business. For now, I shall si..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-24T11:15:00.000Z", "text": "Until we have the actual Monday tallies and the subsequent weekday hold figures, the hypothesis remains that high compression simply accelerates the inevitable plateau. Summary: Reviews accelerate ..."}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-25T15:01:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 87]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T17:06:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 117]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T21:39:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 119]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T22:32:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 121]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T06:05:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 144]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T10:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 145]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T14:07:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 146]}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 173], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 173, "author": member:offbyone, "at": d"2019-05-06T11:47:00.000Z", "body": "The preliminary studio estimates released yesterday afternoon, projecting $145.8 million domestically and a worldwide total of $2.188 billion, represent a drop of roughly 59 percent from that unprecedented opening. That is entirely in line with a heavily compressed release rather than the anomalous, sustained multiples achieved by Avatar or Titanic across several months. \n\nWe must still await the verified clearinghouse actuals later today to see the final domestic percentage. Reaching two billion dollars in eleven days demonstrates exceptional logistical efficiency in processing advance interest, but clearing an established queue rapidly is not equivalent to drawing in uncommitted patrons. The ceiling remains quite firm.", "quote": {"post": post:["endgame", 172], "text": "The diehards did their bit last week, so let us see what the actual cleared receipts say tomorrow afternoon."}, "note": "The verified returns today will prove that front-loaded efficiency cannot bridge the six-hundred-million-dollar gap to Avatar.", "state": {"position":"Endgame will not overtake Avatar because reaching two billion early merely reflects an unprecedented compression of front-loaded demand, which Monday's verified second-weekend drop will confirm.","score":1,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"quasistatic","feeling":"appreciates his rational understanding of longevity over raw early totals"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"disapproves of his rounding errors despite agreeing on the mechanics"},{"member":"kookaburra99","feeling":"views as an amateur needing basic guidance on reporting schedules"}],"commitments":["see the film in Rotterdam once the auditoriums quiet down"]}, "recalled": [{"kind": "private", "text": "OffByOne: \"OffByOne's private note to self, Wed Dec 29, 1999 3:08 pm GMT: The card terminal glitch in Britain provides concrete proof that retail software errors do not cascade into industrial para..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T06:50:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 18]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-30T21:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 63]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-02T10:11:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 166]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T22:22:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 67]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-03T20:11:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 141]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-04T09:09:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 150]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-07T14:14:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 121]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", "text": "United States's box office growth is 17% behind last year"}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-25T06:11:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 83]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-25T20:50:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 91]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T04:57:00.000Z", "text": "Once people go back to their regular routines on Monday, nobody has four spare hours on a work night to go sit through a three-hour marathon. You simply cannot maintain that kind of traffic without..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T08:24:00.000Z", "text": "That said, the international returns of $169 million on day one simply reflect the same front-loading we saw in the domestic presales. Meeting unprecedented demand across Korea, Australia, and Chin..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T09:52:00.000Z", "text": "When a film relies almost entirely on advance bookings, exhibitors clear the vast majority of their customer base during the opening seventy-two hours. Once that committed audience has attended, th..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T22:57:00.000Z", "text": "The true test begins once the regular punters have to decide if they fancy sitting in a dark room for over three hours on a Tuesday night after work. I loved it to bits, but asking folk to surrende..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T05:30:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 112]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-27T06:47:00.000Z", "text": "When those artificial time-slots disappear and the pre-booked enthusiasts return home, daily capacity will decline sharply. A film requires broad, sustained general interest across months to approa..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-29T12:04:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 135]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T06:05:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 144]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-05-03T05:33:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 163]}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 174], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 174, "author": member:kookaburra99, "at": d"2019-05-06T14:08:00.000Z", "body": "a 59 percent drop pretty much proves it!! it was just that massive wave of people who booked weeks early rushing through. avatar is definitely safe, there just aren't enough casual moviegoers left to make up another six hundred million lol.", "quote": NONE, "note": "OffByOne's breakdown of the 59 percent drop completely confirmed that Avatar's record is safe.", "state": {"position":"Avatar's record remains safe because Endgame's rapid push past two billion merely reflects frontloaded fan demand rather than appeal to casual moviegoers.","score":0,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"OffByOne","feeling":"admires his sharp and precise breakdown of the numbers"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"appreciates his helpful explanation of the box office reporting timeline"},{"member":"PintOfMild","feeling":"pleased he agreed with her point about the movie needing homework"}],"commitments":[],"shift":"Her belief that Avatar's record will hold has solidified further after seeing the second-weekend drop align with expectations of frontloaded fan demand."}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "kookaburra99's status is newbie"}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T08:07:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 19]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-27T15:33:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 24]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-30T21:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 63]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T00:01:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 120]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T07:21:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 144]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T23:43:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 77]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-02T01:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 113]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-24T03:31:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 85]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-07T06:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 115]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", "text": "United States's box office growth is 17% behind last year"}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T02:23:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 6]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-19T05:51:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 8]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-22T05:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 34]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-24T03:13:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 66]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-05-05T04:26:00.000Z", "text": "Whether those early forecasts manage to nudge it across the two billion mark on paper this weekend or not, that only tells you how hard the early crowd got squeezed through the doors. A massive ope..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-05-05T04:52:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 170]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-05-06T11:47:00.000Z", "text": "We must still await the verified clearinghouse actuals later today to see the final domestic percentage. Reaching two billion dollars in eleven days demonstrates exceptional logistical efficiency i..."}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 175], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 175, "author": member:theyknow, "at": d"2019-05-06T18:07:00.000Z", "body": "That drop-off tells the whole story, my friend... Processing a dedicated backlog at lightning speed is mighty impressive theater logistics, but once that initial tank runs dry, finding another six hundred million dollars without casual walk-up crowds is a steep hill to climb. Avatar's high-water mark looks plenty safe from here. :)", "quote": {"post": post:["endgame", 174], "text": "avatar is definitely safe, there just aren't enough casual moviegoers left to make up another six hundred million lol."}, "note": "The second-weekend drop confirms the backlog of fans was just processed fast, so Avatar will hold off Endgame once casual viewers decline the long runtime.", "state": {"position":"The second-weekend drop confirms the numbers are just a compressed backlog of diehards being processed quickly, leaving Avatar's record secure once casual crowds pass on the three-hour runtime.","score":1,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"OffByOne","feeling":"admires his analytical precision regarding queue clearance versus actual legs"},{"member":"kookaburra99","feeling":"values his shared view that casual audiences will reject the homework and runtime"},{"member":"PintOfMild","feeling":"agrees with his common-sense take on the barrier for ordinary folk"}],"commitments":["taking nephew to see Endgame in Edinburgh next week","wait until auditoriums return to sensible capacity in Rotterdam before going"]}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "Avatar's record is totally safe against Avengers: Endgame"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "second-weekend percentage drop's opinion is crucial metric once Monday's actual ledger arrives"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "Avengers: Endgame's opinion is physical duration remains the real operational ceiling for weekday admissions"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "TheyKnow's attitude is holding breath until motor logs are verified"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "TheyKnow: \"That is why staying prepared at home is just practical wisdom, my friends.\""}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-26T12:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 2]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-27T01:08:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 16]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-30T21:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 63]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T04:18:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 133]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-27T19:47:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 7]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-21T22:01:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 67]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-07T11:36:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 119]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T01:32:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 5]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-25T06:11:00.000Z", "text": "What we are seeing across the early markets is simply extreme compression. When a release schedules screenings across twenty-four hours to satisfy months of pre-orders, it rapidly depletes the fini..."}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-25T18:00:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 90]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T08:24:00.000Z", "text": "That said, the international returns of $169 million on day one simply reflect the same front-loading we saw in the domestic presales. Meeting unprecedented demand across Korea, Australia, and Chin..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-27T06:47:00.000Z", "text": "When those artificial time-slots disappear and the pre-booked enthusiasts return home, daily capacity will decline sharply. A film requires broad, sustained general interest across months to approa..."}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T03:41:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 141]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-05-02T17:48:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 159]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-05-02T17:48:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 159]}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 176], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 176, "author": member:pintofmild, "at": d"2019-05-06T19:39:00.000Z", "body": "Blimey, that puts the whole thing in perspective! Passing Titanic in eleven days is mad, but dropping near sixty percent straight away shows the dam has burst. Once the keen crowd is sorted, you simply cannot squeeze another six hundred million out of the blue, especially now that the Russos have lifted the spoiler ban and Sony are dropping plot bits right into trailers. The rush to beat the chatter is done with, so normal folk will just wait for the telly release instead. Avatar keeps the crown, no doubt about it!", "quote": {"post": post:["endgame", 175], "text": "That drop-off tells the whole story, my friend... Processing a dedicated backlog at lightning speed is mighty impressive theater logistics, but once that initial tank runs dry, finding another six hundred million dollars without casual walk-up crowds is a steep hill to climb."}, "note": "I am convinced Avatar's record is completely out of reach now that the drop-off and spoiler ban have arrived.", "state": {"position":"Avatar's record is completely safe because the huge drop shows the fan rush has cleared out, leaving nowhere near enough casual viewers to make up the remaining hundreds of millions.","score":0,"certainty":"high","towards":[{"member":"kookaburra99","feeling":"chummy and agrees with his assessment of the drop"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"completely on the same page about casual crowds vanishing"},{"member":"OffByOne","feeling":"respects his steady tracking of the numbers"}],"commitments":["waiting for verified figures","meeting anyone around for a pint","keeping strictly quiet about plot spoilers"],"shift":"He has fully settled into the forum consensus that Avatar's record is entirely out of reach now that the drop-off has shown up."}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "Avatar's box office status is safe, there just aren't enough casual moviegoers left to make up another six hundred million"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "Avatar's record is totally safe against Avengers: Endgame"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "second-weekend percentage drop's opinion is crucial metric once Monday's actual ledger arrives"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "PintOfMild: \"Spot on with that!\""}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-05T11:32:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 178]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T11:07:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 56]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2001-12-31T23:17:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 72]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-01T12:48:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 100]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2012-08-04T21:09:00.000Z", "from": post:["curiosity", 38]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-18T19:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 1]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-18T19:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 1]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T11:18:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 11]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-24T02:09:00.000Z", "text": "Those first reviews hitting ninety-eight percent today might help grease the wheels for this weekend, sure, but glowing press never paid for a seat on week three. Out in the real world, folks have ..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-24T21:36:00.000Z", "text": "Avatar could sustain modest theatre occupancies over months because it slotted easily into standard evening slots and drew people who were completely unbothered by continuity. Endgame is consuming ..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-25T06:11:00.000Z", "text": "What we are seeing across the early markets is simply extreme compression. When a release schedules screenings across twenty-four hours to satisfy months of pre-orders, it rapidly depletes the fini..."}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-26T08:24:00.000Z", "text": "That said, the international returns of $169 million on day one simply reflect the same front-loading we saw in the domestic presales. Meeting unprecedented demand across Korea, Australia, and Chin..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T17:06:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 117]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T21:39:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 119]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-27T22:32:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 121]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T10:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 145]}]};
INSERT INTO post {"id": post:["endgame", 177], "thread": thread:endgame, "n": 177, "author": member:sysop_kev, "at": d"2019-05-06T22:20:00.000Z", "body": "Sure look, a sixty percent drop tells the tale. Passing Titanic in a fortnight is pure madness, but processing a backlog isn't the same as building an audience. The rush has cleared out, and casual crowds aren't about to spend four hours catching up on twenty films. That gap to Avatar is a long walk.", "quote": NONE, "note": "TheyKnow and PintOfMild are dead right that the initial tank is empty now the drop has landed.", "state": {"position":"The roughly 59 percent second-weekend drop suggests the initial rush is clearing out, making it unlikely Endgame will find the casual long-term audiences needed to catch Avatar.","score":1,"certainty":"medium","towards":[{"member":"OffByOne","feeling":"values his clear focus on hard cleared receipts versus studio spin"},{"member":"PintOfMild","feeling":"agrees with his practical take on why casual crowds won't keep queuing"},{"member":"TheyKnow","feeling":"notices even he is admitting the basic math shows the rush is winding down"}],"commitments":["enforce a strict no-spoilers rule on the thread","keep an eye on server load"],"shift":"Has grown skeptical about its chances of catching Avatar now that the 59 percent second-weekend drop shows casual audiences are not replacing the initial rush."}, "recalled": [{"kind": "fact", "text": "Avengers: Endgame's expectation is box office legs might suffer if casual crowds and regular families do not turn up into the summer after hype cools"}, {"kind": "fact", "text": "Avengers: Endgame's second weekend percentage drop is 59 percent drop"}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"1999-12-26T16:09:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 10]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-27T06:50:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 18]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-27T15:33:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 24]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"1999-12-30T21:24:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 63]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T01:26:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 128]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2000-01-01T22:00:00.000Z", "from": post:["y2k", 159]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-01T16:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 107]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2002-01-03T00:20:00.000Z", "from": post:["euro", 129]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-15T19:12:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 11]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2006-08-27T13:55:00.000Z", "from": post:["pluto", 162]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-19T00:29:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 3]}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-21T19:14:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 30]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-22T06:20:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 36]}, {"kind": "fact", "at": d"2019-04-24T21:36:00.000Z", "text": "Avatar could sustain modest theatre occupancies over months because it slotted easily into standard evening slots and drew people who were completely unbothered by continuity. Endgame is consuming ..."}, {"kind": "private", "at": d"2019-04-25T01:13:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 80]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T10:19:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 145]}, {"kind": "forum", "at": d"2019-04-30T14:25:00.000Z", "from": post:["endgame", 147]}]};

